{"arrivo":"tr","origine":"kmr","origine_nome":"Northern Kurdish","n":11,"n_alternative":0,"parole":[{"parola":"-o","pos":"suffix","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"added arbitrarily to words to form slang words","termine_origine":"-o","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"-o","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Northern Kurdish -o (masculine vocative suffix). Doesn't appear in common Turkish speech until the last few decades."},{"parola":"hırbo","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"a brutish, blunt person.","termine_origine":"xirbo","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"xirbo","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Northern Kurdish xirbo (“poor person, beggar”). Compare hırt."},{"parola":"hırt","pos":"adj|noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly; perhaps","significato":"boorish, uncouth; thuggish","termine_origine":"xurt","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"xurt","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"iir-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-Iranian","termine":"*krátuš","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"iir-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Not entirely certain, possibly onomatopoeic. Perhaps related to Northern Kurdish xurt (“vigorous”), itself ultimately from Proto-Indo-Iranian *krátuš. First attested in the 1930s. The reference to Kurds is both a result of a slurred conflation with the term Kürt and a common perception that most peo"},{"parola":"keko","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"a member of a Turkish delinquent subculture, similar to Russian gopniks or British chavs","termine_origine":"kek","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"kek","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from the vocative form of Northern Kurdish kek (“older brother”). Cognate with Persian کاکا (kākā, “older brother, paternal uncle”)."},{"parola":"keleş","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Unknown","significato":"a bald person","termine_origine":"keleş","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"keleş","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Ottoman Turkish کلش (keleş), from Northern Kurdish keleş; further etymology is unknown."},{"parola":"kuzzulkurt","pos":"intj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"","termine_origine":"quzilqurt","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"quzilqurt","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Northern Kurdish quzilqurt."},{"parola":"kıro","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"Any person from Turkey's eastern/southeastern countryside, especially, but not exlusively, Kurdish origin.","termine_origine":"kuro","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"kuro","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Northern Kurdish kuro, vocative of kur (“boy, son”)."},{"parola":"lavuk","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"jerk","termine_origine":"lawik","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"lawik","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Northern Kurdish lawik."},{"parola":"peşmerge","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"peshmerga","termine_origine":"pêşmerge","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"pêşmerge","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Northern Kurdish pêşmerge (“peshmerga”)."},{"parola":"tırrek","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"fool, bloke","termine_origine":"tirek","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"tirek","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"kmr","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Northern Kurdish tirek."},{"parola":"tırsmak","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"to be afraid of, freak out","termine_origine":"tirsîn","catena":[{"codice":"kmr","nome":"Northern Kurdish","termine":"tirsîn","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"ira-pro","nome":"Proto-Iranian","termine":"*tr̥šáti","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"iir-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-Iranian","termine":"*tr̥šćáti","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*tres-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Northern Kurdish tirsîn (“to be afraid of”), from Proto-Iranian *tr̥šáti, from Proto-Indo-Iranian *tr̥šćáti, ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *tres-, first attested in the 1990s. According to Nişanyan the verb spread country-wide from Istanbul slang with Metin Kaçan's book Ağır Roma"}]}